# The entire ~/.claude dir is co-managed by the Claude Code runtime + agent
# environment (settings, enabledPlugins, hooks, plugin state, caches, transcripts
# are all rewritten at runtime). Tracking it caused recurring `chezmoi update`
# conflicts, so the whole directory is left unmanaged.
#
# Exceptions: ~/.claude/output-styles/*.md holds portable, machine-independent
# output styles that Claude Code loads at user scope, and ~/.claude/themes/*.json
# holds the custom themes (cozycabin is the Quartz claude-code palette; see
# quartz/custom.scss). Nothing rewrites the output styles at runtime. Only the
# `/theme` editor (Ctrl+E on a custom theme) rewrites a theme file, so edit the
# source here, or `chezmoi re-add` the file after using the editor. Re-including
# a child needs the parent glob (`.claude/*`) and an explicit un-ignore of each
# directory on the way down; a bare `.claude` ignore cannot be negated.
.claude/*
!.claude/output-styles
.claude/output-styles/*
!.claude/output-styles/*.md
!.claude/themes
.claude/themes/*
!.claude/themes/*.json

# The Quartz site that renders the work vault (the `daily` command) reads its
# config and styles from quartz/ in the source dir. dot_config/
# symlink_quartz-vault.tmpl links ~/.config/quartz-vault to that folder, and
# quartz/setup.sh links the files into the Quartz clone at
# ~/.local/share/quartz.
quartz
quartz/**
